    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83991.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Yes, no, I don't. I don't either. But in fact, you would be wondering with this administration. It feels like they're trying to buddy up to Iran or Iran or whatever you want to call it. It's bad news. Obviously, we saw this over the weekend with the unprecedented, again, I hate that word, but the never-before-seen direct attack on Israel from Iran, the way that they had conducted that over the weekend. We came back to Washington. Actually, I came back early on Monday to be a part of a floor debate about sanctions on Iran. The problem with this administration right now is that they have softened and rolled back sanctions that have been put on Iran over number of years, even predating President Trump. So what we saw with the Trump administration was the maximum pressure, and this has been maximum appeasement. They're trying everything they can to get them pulled back into the world stage.",
